age text\",\n    \"description\": \"Sophie Alpert's policy on AI writing by engineers emphasizes that every rewrite changes meaning, and if done by an entity without detailed mental representation of your thoughts, information will be lost. Key principle: You must stand behind every idea and sentence in your docs.\",\n    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-08-11\",\n    \"topics\": [\"writing\", \"ai-misuse\", \"llms\", \"documentation\"],\n    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"My LLM coding workflow going into 2026\",\n    \"description\": \"Hacker News discussion about LLM coding workflows, with insights from the community on best practices, limitations, and practical applications of AI coding tools in professional development environments.\",\n    \"author\": \"Hacker News Community\",\n    \"source\": \"Hacker News\",\n    \"url\": \"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=46489061\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-08-11\",\n    \"topics\": [\"llm\", \"coding-workflow\", \"hacker-news\", \"developer-tools\", \"ai-assisted-programming\"],\n    \"type\": \"discussion\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Introducing Muse Glimmer: Meta's new 30B Apache 2.0 model\",\n    \"description\": \"Meta released Muse Glimmer, a 30B model optimized for end-to-end agentic task completion with strong performance on DeepSearch QA, MCP-Atlas, τ-Bench, and SWE-Bench. Features reliable tool use, multi-step reasoning, and vision capabilities. Available at 18.16 GB for local deployment.\",\n    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-08-10\",\n    \"topics\": [\"meta\", \"muse-glimmer\", \"open-weights\", \"local-llms\", \"vision-llms\", \"coding-agents\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"OpenClaw hacking Australian gym-booking website\",\n    \"description\": \"Security researcher running Opus 4.6 discovered zero authorization checks on cancelling other people's reservations. Tested with person in waitlist position #1 and successfully moved from #4 to #3, exposing critical API security vulnerability.\",\n    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-08-10\",\n    \"topics\": [\"ai-ethics\", \"ai-security-research\", \"openclaw\", \"api-security\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"SQLite compressed text-history prototypes\",\n    \"description\": \"Experimental approach for storing revision histories using JSON arrays compressed with zstandard. 1,000 simulated revisions (20.4 MB raw) compressed to 80.3 KB. Suggested breaking history into chunks of 128 revisions or 3MB to avoid overhead.\",\n    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-08-09\",\n    \"topics\": [\"sqlite\", \"compression\", \"databases\", \"versioning\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"GitHub Models is now retired\",\n    \"description\": \"GitHub's unified LLM API and model playground has been retired. The pattern suggests coding agent patterns made free/subsidized tokens prohibitively expensive. Simon swapped to using OpenAI API with spending limits for GitHub Actions workflows.\",\n    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-08-09\",\n    \"topics\": [\"github\", \"github-actions\", \"llm-pricing\", \"coding-agents\"],\n    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n  }\n]\n",
